WEBVTT

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.540
I finally know what my target is.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.360
I'm going to have you proceed directly.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.940
Clash! The Two Formidable Enemies

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.640
Okay, I'll be taking my leave here.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.020
I have something to do.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.290
Something to do?

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.970
Are you going to buy curry bread?

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.150
No.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.250
They have a cream curry bread 
available today only.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:19.950
They'll sell out if I don't hurry.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.520
Wow, today only?

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.160
Well, that's important.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.450
See you.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.250
Uh... Um...

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.010
Oh, no...

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.310
What's wrong?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:53.140
I-I'm looking for something.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.320
What are you looking for?

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.470
I-It's, like, this small card.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.660
I've been looking for it, but... 
Oh, man, this is a problem...

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.040
Do you want me to help you look?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.460
Huh? Oh, no, that's okay.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.210
Thank you for asking.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.340
Okay.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.680
Um, wa—

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.210
Please wait!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:26.100
Your kindness has been 
carved deep into my heart.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:26.800
Okay...

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.610
Thank you very much.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.700
You're welcome.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.230
I-I'll be going, then.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.970
I... I did it.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:43.360
Ya—

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.750
I extended my leg too suddenly,
and it cramped up.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.590
I'm back.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.340
Welcome back.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.910
Food's almost ready.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.440
Okay.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.860
Why the long face?

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.930
Well...

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.740
Oh, welcome back, Sato-chin.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.720
Did you get that today-only 
cream curry bread?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.390
Excellent
Curry Bread

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.390
Well, I was able to buy it, but...

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.930
I could only buy one!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.360
<i>...one!</i>

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.700
The person in line before me got two, 
so there was only one left...

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.080
If I hadn't talked to that girl, 
I could have gotten three.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.080
That girl?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.640
I think I've seen her before, but...

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.420
So what was she looking for?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.280
A card-like thing.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.130
Card? A trading card?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.960
From what she told me, 
it sounded like something smaller.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.060
A Memoca?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.660
That can't be.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.470
Yeah, that's not it.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.600
That's true.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.810
A girl who isn't in Fifth Force 
shouldn't know about Memoca.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.270
Memoca?

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:53.840
Yes.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.640
Moshune-chan said she'd get me one,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.260
but I was wondering what it was.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.230
Specifically speaking,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.880
it's a device that collects information 
in the rift between dimensions, moshu.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.040
Information?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.660
Mostly technological information.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.110
The weapons and armor that 
the Fifth Force wears

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.550
are produced using this information.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:20.680
You can also make changes and 
add new functions to them, moshu.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:27.420
So does that mean that the weapons 
and powers we get aren't of this world?

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:27.840
Yes.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:35.020
That's the only method we have to resist 
the O'bli available to us in this world.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.420
<i>Technology from another world...</i>

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.100
Tsubame, what's wrong?

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.390
Huh? Oh, nothing.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:45.240
Just thinking it'd be nice if we could get 
stronger without relying on Memoca.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.720
Yeah...

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.390
We can improve our Memoca, but we can't 
catch up to the other teams with that alone.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.660
How about we try training again?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.730
Good idea!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:55.730
I agree!

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.500
As long as we don't have to swim...

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.050
Yeah! That sounds good!

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.000
What type of training should we do this time?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.000
Something close to real combat would be good.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.170
Real combat...

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.220
I know!

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.760
Okay, thank you.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.230
Roger, moshu.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.640
Activating the Stella Prism, moshu.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:19.910
Training in the boundary...

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:22.110
That'll definitely feel like real combat.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:27.330
I chose a dimensional stable point, so 
there won't be any O'bli appearing, moshu.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.440
Go train to your hearts' content.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:55.390
There are no people in the boundary.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.460
We can use our weapons all we want.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.020
We can go as wild as we want!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:02.500
It's true this is the best place to train.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.860
Good job, Leader.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.340
I've thought of a training program, too.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.150
Thank you.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.710
There won't be any enemies 
like in the simulations,

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.590
but we can move around all we 
want in our transformed states!

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.010
Yeah!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.640
Torte really likes their training.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.200
Sweat and tears, friendship and hard work.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.130
That's what makes Altair Torte great, moshu.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:28.490
They're not on top, by any means,

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.130
but they're running towards 
the setting sun right now, moshu.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.130
They're running while transformed...

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.930
Altair Torte is the best!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.180
Altair Torte is the best!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:45.150
We won't lose to our rival teams!

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.940
We won't lose to our rival teams!

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:01.330
We are getting our exercise in,
but it feels kind of different...

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.420
Wh-What was that?

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.460
A laugh?

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.620
Do people laugh like that?

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.880
There isn't supposed to be 
anyone here but us.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.240
Could it be an O'bli?

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:16.640
But there aren't any 
dimensional distortions...

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.640
No, that's not quite right.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.520
Who is that?!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.180
Where are they?

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:22.810
Where are they?

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.480
Where are they?

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.360
Forget that.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.800
Over there!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.200
Yeah, that was better.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.990
Wh-What?

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:38.110
Here I am!

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:41.700
I am the lone soldier who travels the 
rough path between time and space.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.500
I don wings of darkness on my shoulders.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.610
My name is the Knight 
of the Black Swan, Odile!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.160
Odile?

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:52.550
Knight of the Black Mongoose?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.740
Black Swan! Not Mongoose!

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.680
I don't have a tail!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.140
Nice to meet you all.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.850
Oh, thank you.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.600
Now, all of you, give me the Stella Prism.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.940
Stella Prism?

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:07.680
It's no use hiding it.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:13.860
I know you're using the Stella Prism 
to travel the dimensions.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:18.720
I knew it existed, but I've finally 
figured out the coordinates.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.580
You can't get away any longer.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.610
Now, hand it over. Hand it over!

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.990
And hand all of the Memoca 
that you have over, too!

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.960
We can't just do that...

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.290
Don't play dumb!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.840
Then why don't you jump for me?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:32.870
Okay!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.670
She's trying to extort us!

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.870
We can't hand over the 
Stella Prism or our Memoca.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:42.060
We're not supposed to get 
robbed in the boundary.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.160
Who're you calling a robber?

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.180
It goes against reason.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.800
The distortions it creates 
in the dimensions...

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.190
Uh... I forget.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.250
Anyway, just hand it over!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.530
She talks too much.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:58.420
If you resist, I'll take them by force.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.870
Odile kick!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.560
If you don't want to get hurt, 
give me all your mon—

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.980
I mean, Memoca and the Stella Prism.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.710
You <i>are</i> a robber!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.820
Looks like we'll just have to fight.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:19.590
Yeah.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.730
That won't work!

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:36.190
Upper!

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:43.740
Wh-Who is this girl?

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.500
She didn't seem serious, but...

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.460
She's really strong.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:58.470
Is that all the Fifth Force can do?

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.220
In that case, I'll just end this now.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.640
She's using all her weapons at once?

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:08.050
Oh, no!

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.390
I can't use a bow like this!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.560
Yeah, that makes sense.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.370
I was just trying to show off, that's all!

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.070
Well? You were surprised, right?

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.820
In any event, prepare yourself!

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.110
Everyone, run!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:30.660
Crap! My leg cramped!

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.560
D-Damn it.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:40.650
You're good!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.750
I'll let you off the hook for today!

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:44.470
I'll be back!

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.540
Ow... My leg hurts.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.390
I-I guess we're safe?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.480
What was that?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.050
I don't know...

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.990
Odile?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.540
She said she was the 
Knight of the Black Mongoose.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.710
Knight of the Black Swan, Satoka-chan.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:14.740
What's that?

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.040
Sounds like a very elegant name.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:20.100
If that's true, I'd like to see her once.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.970
No, it's not a joke. It's true.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.900
She talked funny, but she was really strong.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:27.550
Right?

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.640
Yeah.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.760
She ran away for some reason, 
so we ended up fine, but...

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.350
She was fast running away, too.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.100
She's fast?!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.510
I want to race her!

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:39.340
I understand the O'bli,

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.780
but why can a human who's not part of 
the Fifth Force appear in the barrier?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.120
Tierra-sensei asked the same thing.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:52.120
We were just training, and there wasn't 
anything weird, so she didn't monitor it.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.380
So does that mean she appeared without 
accompanying a dimensional distortion?

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.590
That can't happen without a Stella Prism.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.510
But she was really there!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.700
She appeared out of nowhere 
and left out of nowhere,

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.800
so we didn't have time to contact anyone.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.900
Amane, we need to get going.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:09.810
Yeah.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:14.350
Well, we're going on patrol now.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.230
Watch out for Odile.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.520
We'll let you know.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.530
They don't believe us at all, huh?

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.150
That makes sense.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.840
Who is the Knight of the 
Black Mongoose, anyway?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.540
Satoka-chan, are you doing that on purpose?

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:39.150
The area around the transfer point is stable,

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.200
but stay alert as you do your patrol.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.000
Roger.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:43.990
Hey.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:44.620
Yes?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.470
We heard from Altair Torte

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.680
about the Knight of the Black Swan, Odile...

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.370
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.090
It's hard to believe 
someone like that exists,

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.400
but there are records of weapons being used.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:00.810
Records...

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:04.920
It was training, so it's difficult 
to say for sure.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.580
If I had some harder evidence...

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.780
Be careful just in case.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:13.370
Procyon Pudding is going on patrol.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:22.290
Nothing seems out of place here.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.170
I wish that Odile would show up.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.090
I'd have to run a 100-meter race with her!

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.050
Maybe they had a weird dream due to some 
weird effect from the parallel worlds.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.680
Mano, what's wrong?

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:46.900
Over there.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:47.970
An O'bli?

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.680
Found you.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:50.660
It's you guys, right?

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:51.820
She talked!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:52.620
Humans?

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:56.370
If you get in our way, sorry, 
but we won't hold back.

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:57.550
Um...

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:00.170
Are you Odile-san?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:00.620
Huh?

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.270
There aren't supposed to be three of you.

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.130
Who is that? What are you talking about?

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.480
Mano, contact Eterno.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.010
Roger.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.360
Hey, don't play dumb.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:12.140
You're going around taking out 
the O'bli we're placing out here.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.140
Wh-What was that?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:18.060
You're the ones sending the 
O'bli into the boundary?

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:18.980
That's right.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.530
It is the important mission with 
which we have been charged.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.320
We didn't detect any dimensional 
distortions at all, moshu.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.240
Then the three of them...

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:30.560
They likely transferred there 
via Stella Prism, moshu.

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:32.260
What teams are available to sortie?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.370
Vega and Sirius are on patrol, moshu.

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.370
Get Altair Torte out there.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.050
They have the same abilities as us?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.380
Who are you all?

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.090
It doesn't matter!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.090
Disperse!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:56.720
Amane!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:03.210
Over here.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.310
No, over here.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:06.980
She reflected it?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.120
You have to be thorough 
when you do something.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.620
U-Um...

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.720
Going halfway will make no one happy.

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.000
Altair Torte is here.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:27.530
Sensei?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.480
Pudding!

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.200
Wh-What's going on?

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.510
What's happening?

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:37.760
What happened?

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.640
Jeez, what was up with them?

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:48.030
We had no information,
and they got the jump on us.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.080
We couldn't help it.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.440
We'll get them good next time.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.810
We really got taken out.

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:57.740
At least pretend you're being serious!

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:02.110
Being serious isn't going to 
change the truth, though.

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:05.420
I wonder if they had something to do with 
the Odile that Torte was talking about.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:09.130
We can't just laugh this off, though.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:14.800
In any event, they had the same abilities 
as the Fifth Force, that's for sure, moshu.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.860
So that means Stella Prisms and 
Memoca exist outside of Eterno?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.640
That would be right, moshu.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:25.940
These three aren't the ones 
who attacked you, right?

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:28.560
Right, it wasn't them.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:32.320
Odile hid her face, but her voice 
was completely different.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.960
She moved differently, too.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:34.780
Mana?

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.970
I know them...

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:36.600
Huh?

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.320
I know these girls.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.830
You know them?

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.250
Yeah, it was when I was younger...

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.910
But it has to be them.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:47.290
When I was at the orphanage, 
there were three girls always together.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.880
Uh, their names were... Origami...

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.150
Oh, this girl is Akara-chin.

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.070
She's the eldest sister.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.590
Her little sisters are Hina-chin and Koori-chin.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.410
Ow...

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:12.440
Mana-chan was in an orphanage 
when she was younger.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.030
She got into Goryoukan Academy via 
an assistant program, supposedly.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.890
I see.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.740
But why would girls from 
the same orphanage be here?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.470
They're not on our side, either.

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:26.830
Those three sisters and Odile...

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.970
Strong enemies keep popping up!

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.740
I guess you call this being as busy as a bee.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.960
I understand what you're trying to say.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:39.590
When I was in the orphanage, 
the three went missing.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.120
Missing?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.190
Yeah.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.460
I remember they went missing all of a sudden.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:49.350
I think it was a little 
before I met you, Io-chin.

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.340
Me?

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.860
Oh yeah, you used to 
get teased a lot and cry.

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:57.700
But that was good.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:58.830
Good?

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.860
It was because I was getting teased...

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.850
That's why I met you.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.300
You were so cool.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:15.420
You know, I thought you were a boy.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.470
What? Really?

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.430
Yeah.

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:21.290
I thought you were my prince.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:26.200
Well, I had short hair. 
I got mistaken for a boy a lot.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.770
Sorry for ruining your dreams.

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:31.850
You're still my prince, Io-chin.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:37.070
When I was crying at the park, 
you'd always come to my rescue.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.250
Do you remember the promise 
we made back then?

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.420
Promise?

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.660
Huh? What was it?

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:46.960
Hey!

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:49.750
You promised to protect me 
no matter what happened.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.120
Oh, I see.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.750
I guess I did promise that.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.760
You're still going to keep that promise, right?

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:58.290
You're doing fine by yourself now.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.240
No, that's not it.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:05.170
If it comes down to it, 
I need you to save me.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.170
Please.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.210
Very well.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.950
Leave it to me, Princess.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:15.400
Just kidding.

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.220
That was really good!

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.050
Io-chin!

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:26.350
You haven't changed at all, Mana.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:30.100
I wonder why Akara-chin 
and the others changed.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:34.960
I wonder why we can't all get along 
like when we were younger.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.080
Mana...

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.090
I'm sure we can.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:41.090
You're right!

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:45.090
I don't know what's going 
on with them right now.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.060
I don't know what will happen.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:49.220
But they're your childhood friends.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.720
You'll be able to get along 
with them again someday.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:54.020
You have to believe in that and try hard.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.560
Yeah. Yeah.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.340
I'll try hard!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.780
You got your target wrong.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.650
What?

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:07.100
Weren't we supposed to 
take out the Fifth Force?

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.530
I told you there were four teams.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.710
I thought we just needed 
to take out all of them.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.320
They seemed kind of strong.

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.500
That doesn't matter.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:20.890
Your target is Altair Torte alone.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.680
Your punishment will be going without dinner.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:33.430
My legs cramp up when things get important.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.630
It's because I'm scared of talking to people.

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:39.650
That's why I did image training 
for two weeks straight...

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:42.050
I finally got to one of them

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:45.240
and traced the coordinates, but...

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:50.660
Why can't I do anything right?

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:54.660
But I can't give up now.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:57.170
Please watch me.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:22:00.930
I'm going to destroy all the Memoca

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:03.400
and Stella Prisms on my own.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
Showdown! The Three Origami Sisters

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:40.690
"Showdown! The Three Origami Sisters."
